  'escrow.nets.title': 'Networks with escrow available',
  'escrow.nets.note': 'The contract must be deployed on the chosen network. If the network has no support yet, the app warns you and notifies the manager to prioritize the deploy.',
  'escrow.faq.title': 'Frequently asked questions',
  'escrow.faq.1.title': 'What if the arbitrator disappears?',
  'escrow.faq.1.desc': 'The deadline resolves it: once expired, <code>refundExpired</code> returns the funds to the payer. Nothing stays blocked.',
  'escrow.faq.2.title': 'Can the arbitrator steal?',
  'escrow.faq.2.desc': 'No. The arbitrator only decides the direction (receiver or payer) — the contract never releases funds to the arbitrator, only the arbitration fee.',
  'escrow.faq.3.title': 'Can I have 2 arbitrators later?',
  'escrow.faq.3.desc': 'Yes — before confirming readiness, the receiver can request a second arbitrator at any time.',
  'escrow.faq.4.title': 'Which coins?',
  'escrow.faq.4.desc': 'All the ones the app supports on the network: native coin (ETH, POL…) and ERC-20 tokens (USDC, BRLA, BRZ, RAI…).',
  'escrow.faq.5.title': 'Who controls the contract?',
  'escrow.faq.5.desc': 'Administration is done by a Rapport 2-of-3 multisig; upgrades go through quorum, never a single key.',
  'escrow.faq.6.title': 'Is the escrow private?',
  'escrow.faq.6.desc': 'Messages are end-to-end encrypted between participants. On-chain there are only addresses, amounts and decisions — no personal data.',
